# FAQ usage — oka

Before answering questions about this repo, route to the right doc:

| Question type | Read |
|---|---|
| **Why** is it designed this way? | `docs/DESIGN_FAQ.mdx`, then `docs/decisions/` (ADRs) |
| **How** do I run/build/test/ship? | `docs/DX_FAQ.mdx` (Memory Palace), then `docs/guides/build_and_config.mdx` for depth |
| What does oka own / not own? | `docs/start_here/why_this_repo_matters.mdx` |
| Newcomer what/who/prerequisites | `docs/FAQ.md` |
| Phase status / evidence | `docs/PHASE_CHECKLIST.mdx` |
| Behavior of code | The code and tests themselves — docs only link |

## DESIGN vs DX vs ADRs

- **ADRs** (`docs/decisions/`) record significant, reviewable decisions.
- **DESIGN_FAQ** compresses standing **why** answers; link to ADRs for full deliberation.
- **DX_FAQ** compresses **how** with copy-paste CLI blocks — no duplicated rationale.
- **build_and_config** and topic guides remain long-form; FAQs do not replace them.

## Package-level FAQs

Root FAQs cover the monorepo charter and CLI today. Packages with distinct
design boundaries may later add their own `DESIGN_FAQ` / `DX_FAQ` pairs; parent
FAQs should only route (no repeated answers). Candidates: `oka_dart_kernel`
(kernel graph / live gates), `oka_update` (patch units), `oka_process` (owned
POSIX sessions).

Rules:

- Never paraphrase implementation in answers; link to the authoritative file.
- After changing architecture → add/update a Q&A in `docs/DESIGN_FAQ.mdx` (or ADR).
- After changing commands/API usage → update `docs/DX_FAQ.mdx` and, if needed, `docs/guides/build_and_config.mdx`.
- Design forks require a decision checkpoint + ADR before coding.
- Do not duplicate paragraphs between DESIGN_FAQ and DX_FAQ—link instead.